      "fontSize": 42.681479480127855,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "Resource Allocation/Capacity Management System",
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Resource Allocation/Capacity Management System",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ZwlrSBbTlWKy9nr4P6vQB",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 514.086919336999,
      "y": 73036.07532788345,
      "width": 1540.8729084670078,
      "height": 2509.6962860169288,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bNw",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1609344734,
      "version": 1150,
      "versionNonce": 1996162734,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788724199374,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "DB: \nRESOURCE\nPurpose: Authoritative record for each allocatable resource and \nits current ownership/capacity state.\n\n- resourceId — unique ID of the machine/resource being allocated.\n- poolKey — identifies the placement pool this resource belongs to, \n         such as us-west-2 / AZ-1 / GPU; used to quickly narrow candidate \n         searches instead of scanning all resources.\n- cpuTotal — total CPU capacity this resource can provide.\n- memoryTotal — total memory capacity this resource can provide.\n- state — tells whether this resource can currently be selected: \n             AVAILABLE, RESERVED, ALLOCATED, etc.\n- version — increments whenever the resource state changes; an allocator updates \n    the resource only if the version it read is still current, preventing two allocators \n    from successfully claiming the same resource.\n\nALLOCATION\nPurpose: Tracks one customer's allocation request from reservation \nthrough provisioning/release.\n\n- allocationId — unique ID for this allocation request; also lets \n                retries refer to the same allocation.\n- tenantId — customer that owns the allocation; used for \n                quotas, priority, and fairness.\n- resourceId — resource successfully selected/reserved for this allocation.\n- state — current lifecycle stage, such as \n            RESERVED, PROVISIONING, ACTIVE, FAILED, or RELEASED.\n- expiresAt — time after which an unfinished reservation can be reclaimed \n        so capacity is not leaked forever.\n- requestHash — fingerprint of the important request parameters; if the \n        same request ID is retried with different parameters, we can detect \n        that it is not the same logical request.\n\nCAPACITY_POOL\nPurpose: Small summary of capacity for a placement pool, used to decide \n        which pools are worth searching before looking at individual resources.\n\n- poolKey — identifies a pool such as region + AZ + resource class.\n- availableCount — approximate number of currently available resources in \n                    that pool; helps skip pools that are likely full.\n- capacityClass — normalized/bucketed capacity characteristics used to \n                    match requests to suitable pools.\n- updatedAt — when this summary was last refreshed; lets the allocator \n                judge whether the approximate capacity information may be stale.\n\nAVAILABILITY_INDEX\nPurpose: Derived lookup structure containing currently usable resource candidates \n            so allocation does not scan the authoritative RESOURCE table.\n\n- poolKey — pool under which this resource is searchable.\n- resourceId — candidate resource that may satisfy an allocation request.\n- freeCpu — CPU currently believed to be available on this candidate.\n- freeMemory — memory currently believed to be available on this candidate.\n- version — RESOURCE version from when this index entry was created; helps \n          detect that the index entry is stale relative to authoritative resource state.",
      "fontSize": 35.85280408595611,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "DB: \nRESOURCE\nPurpose: Authoritative record for each allocatable resource and \nits current ownership/capacity state.\n\n- resourceId — unique ID of the machine/resource being allocated.\n- poolKey — identifies the placement pool this resource belongs to, \n         such as us-west-2 / AZ-1 / GPU; used to quickly narrow candidate \n         searches instead of scanning all resources.\n- cpuTotal — total CPU capacity this resource can provide.\n- memoryTotal — total memory capacity this resource can provide.\n- state — tells whether this resource can currently be selected: \n             AVAILABLE, RESERVED, ALLOCATED, etc.\n- version — increments whenever the resource state changes; an allocator updates \n    the resource only if the version it read is still current, preventing two allocators \n    from successfully claiming the same resource.\n\nALLOCATION\nPurpose: Tracks one customer's allocation request from reservation \nthrough provisioning/release.\n\n- allocationId — unique ID for this allocation request; also lets \n                retries refer to the same allocation.\n- tenantId — customer that owns the allocation; used for \n                quotas, priority, and fairness.\n- resourceId — resource successfully selected/reserved for this allocation.\n- state — current lifecycle stage, such as \n            RESERVED, PROVISIONING, ACTIVE, FAILED, or RELEASED.\n- expiresAt — time after which an unfinished reservation can be reclaimed \n        so capacity is not leaked forever.\n- requestHash — fingerprint of the important request parameters; if the \n        same request ID is retried with different parameters, we can detect \n        that it is not the same logical request.\n\nCAPACITY_POOL\nPurpose: Small summary of capacity for a placement pool, used to decide \n        which pools are worth searching before looking at individual resources.\n\n- poolKey — identifies a pool such as region + AZ + resource class.\n- availableCount — approximate number of currently available resources in \n                    that pool; helps skip pools that are likely full.\n- capacityClass — normalized/bucketed capacity characteristics used to \n                    match requests to suitable pools.\n- updatedAt — when this summary was last refreshed; lets the allocator \n                judge whether the approximate capacity information may be stale.\n\nAVAILABILITY_INDEX\nPurpose: Derived lookup structure containing currently usable resource candidates \n            so allocation does not scan the authoritative RESOURCE table.\n\n- poolKey — pool under which this resource is searchable.\n- resourceId — candidate resource that may satisfy an allocation request.\n- freeCpu — CPU currently believed to be available on this candidate.\n- freeMemory — memory currently believed to be available on this candidate.\n- version — RESOURCE version from when this index entry was created; helps \n          detect that the index entry is stale relative to authoritative resource state.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "u0C569CqgogtojFAPL4Vp",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 498.3745639241397,
      "y": 71161.9344530086,
      "width": 1398.9931934629403,
      "height": 1119.8819011410264,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bNy",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1150131650,
      "version": 535,
      "versionNonce": 327287022,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788724199374,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "FR: \n- Allocate a resource that satisfies CPU, memory, resource-type, region/AZ, \n  and tenant constraints.\n- Guarantee exclusivity — no two concurrent requests can claim the same resource.\n- Release & reclaim — free resources on request, and reclaim \n   reservations abandoned without provisioning/heartbeat.\n- Track lifecycle — every resource moves through \n   Available → Reserved → Provisioning → Allocated → Released, \n   with state transitions observable.\n\nNon-FR\n- Handle bursts of concurrent allocation requests/traffic.\n- Strong consistency for the final resource claim; \n  stale reads are acceptable during candidate discovery.\n- Low allocation latency without scanning the full inventory.\n\nBACK-OF-THE-ENVELOPE: \nAssume 10M managed resources.\nPeak burst: 500K allocation requests / 10 sec\n            ≈ 50K allocation attempts/sec.\n\nIf each request examines only ~20 candidates:\n        50K × 20 ≈ 1M candidate evaluations/sec.\n\nResource state ~1 KB × 10M\n≈ 10 GB logical metadata, easily partitionable.",
      "fontSize": 34.45790465049312,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "FR: \n- Allocate a resource that satisfies CPU, memory, resource-type, region/AZ, \n  and tenant constraints.\n- Guarantee exclusivity — no two concurrent requests can claim the same resource.\n- Release & reclaim — free resources on request, and reclaim \n   reservations abandoned without provisioning/heartbeat.\n- Track lifecycle — every resource moves through \n   Available → Reserved → Provisioning → Allocated → Released, \n   with state transitions observable.\n\nNon-FR\n- Handle bursts of concurrent allocation requests/traffic.\n- Strong consistency for the final resource claim; \n  stale reads are acceptable during candidate discovery.\n- Low allocation latency without scanning the full inventory.\n\nBACK-OF-THE-ENVELOPE: \nAssume 10M managed resources.\nPeak burst: 500K allocation requests / 10 sec\n            ≈ 50K allocation attempts/sec.\n\nIf each request examines only ~20 candidates:\n        50K × 20 ≈ 1M candidate evaluations/sec.\n\nResource state ~1 KB × 10M\n≈ 10 GB logical metadata, easily partitionable.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "MCY9VhOiL5Hzx1HX11NqU",
