    {
      "id": "6FaUL1dYuVT-a44smFCGw",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3260.9355364239354,
      "y": 72014.13830553088,
      "width": 397.66081820256977,
      "height": 102.29836576866586,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bOz",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 590658427,
      "version": 694,
      "versionNonce": 599041198,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788724199375,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Async state changes\n(CDC / async index update/Outbox)\nWhenever a resource update perdformed\nCDC event fired to update Redis",
      "fontSize": 20.459673153733174,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Async state changes\n(CDC / async index update/Outbox)\nWhenever a resource update perdformed\nCDC event fired to update Redis",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Rke45pGr8S5Ue7z2vsBrN",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2377.7053903918463,
      "y": 72014.94809210101,
      "width": 329.1925214869825,
      "height": 451.14897326523067,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bP1",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1980146363,
      "version": 464,
      "versionNonce": 1935138542,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788724199375,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Full Flow is:       \n       candidate lookup\nAllocator ------------------------> Redis\n   |                                 |\n   | returns r101,r102,r108          |\n   |<--------------------------------+\n   |\n   | CAS r101\n   v\nAuthoritative DB\n   |\n   | AVAILABLE → RESERVED\n   |\n   +------ change event / CDC ------+\n                                    |\n                                    v\n                              Index Updater\n                                    |\n                                    v\n                                  Redis\n                              remove r101",
      "fontSize": 17.18662755296118,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Full Flow is:       \n       candidate lookup\nAllocator ------------------------> Redis\n   |                                 |\n   | returns r101,r102,r108          |\n   |<--------------------------------+\n   |\n   | CAS r101\n   v\nAuthoritative DB\n   |\n   | AVAILABLE → RESERVED\n   |\n   +------ change event / CDC ------+\n                                    |\n                                    v\n                              Index Updater\n                                    |\n                                    v\n                                  Redis\n                              remove r101",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "XjdwwavZHN9urgBgKihG6",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4794.699007486506,
      "y": 73182.51859299841,
      "width": 851.7739414165902,
      "height": 2440.9977172639205,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bQm",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 375957237,
      "version": 1209,
      "versionNonce": 1461309742,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788724199375,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The Availability Index stores a fast-searchable, derived view of \nresources that appear available so Placement Allocator does not \nquery/scan the authoritative Resource DB for every allocation request.\n\nA good mental model is:\n\nAuthoritative DB = truth\nAvailability Index = fast lookup/cache of candidates\nWhere can the Availability Index live?\n\nFor this design, Redis is a very reasonable choice, especially in a 30-minute interview.\n\nFor example, partition it by poolKey:\n\npoolKey = us-west-2#az-a#compute-large\n\n        ↓\n\nRedis\n---------------------------------\nr101 → cpu=8,  memory=32, version=17\nr102 → cpu=16, memory=64, version=12\nr103 → cpu=8,  memory=64, version=21\n\nThen the allocator can quickly ask:\n\nGive me candidates from:\nus-west-2 / AZ-A / compute-large\n\ninstead of querying millions of Resource records.\n\nDepending on the exact search requirements, alternatives \ncould be DynamoDB secondary indexes, OpenSearch, or another \npurpose-built in-memory/index structure. For the interview, \nRedis/sharded in-memory index is easy to explain.\n\n\nBut how does Redis know which resources are available?\n\nThis is the more important part.\nI would not make a periodic full DB-scanning job the primary mechanism.\n\nInstead, update the Availability Index asynchronously whenever authoritative Resource state changes.\n\nThink:\n              authoritative change\n                     |\n                     v\nResource DB ----> change event / CDC ----> Index Updater ----> Redis\n\nFor example, initially:\n\nRESOURCE DB\nr101\nstate = AVAILABLE\ncpu = 8\nmemory = 32\nversion = 17\n\nThe index updater gets that change and adds:\nRedis:\npoolKey → r101\nNow r101 becomes discoverable.\nWhen the resource is reserved\nAllocator performs the authoritative CAS:\n\nr101:\nAVAILABLE/v17\n      ↓\nRESERVED/v18\n\nThe database is updated first.\n\nThen that change eventually reaches the index updater:\n\nDB change:\nr101 RESERVED\n      ↓\nIndex Updater\n      ↓\nremove r101 from Redis availability index\n\nSo eventually:\n\nRedis no longer contains r101\n\nThere can be a short period where Redis still says r101 is available.\n\nThat's exactly why we say:\n\nThe availability index may be stale.\n\nWhat happens during that stale window?\n\nSuppose:\n\nDB:\nr101 = RESERVED/v18\n\nRedis:\nr101 = AVAILABLE/v17    ← hasn't caught up yet\n\nAnother allocator searches Redis.\n\nRedis returns:\n\nr101\n\nThat's fine.\n\nThe allocator then goes to the authoritative DB:\n\nclaim r101\nif state == AVAILABLE\nand version == 17\n\nBut the DB contains:\n\nRESERVED/v18\n\nSo CAS fails.\n\nAllocator simply tries another top-K candidate:\n\nr102\n\nThis is why the design works even when Redis is eventually consistent.\n\n",
      "fontSize": 15.137970339621212,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The Availability Index stores a fast-searchable, derived view of \nresources that appear available so Placement Allocator does not \nquery/scan the authoritative Resource DB for every allocation request.\n\nA good mental model is:\n\nAuthoritative DB = truth\nAvailability Index = fast lookup/cache of candidates\nWhere can the Availability Index live?\n\nFor this design, Redis is a very reasonable choice, especially in a 30-minute interview.\n\nFor example, partition it by poolKey:\n\npoolKey = us-west-2#az-a#compute-large\n\n        ↓\n\nRedis\n---------------------------------\nr101 → cpu=8,  memory=32, version=17\nr102 → cpu=16, memory=64, version=12\nr103 → cpu=8,  memory=64, version=21\n\nThen the allocator can quickly ask:\n\nGive me candidates from:\nus-west-2 / AZ-A / compute-large\n\ninstead of querying millions of Resource records.\n\nDepending on the exact search requirements, alternatives \ncould be DynamoDB secondary indexes, OpenSearch, or another \npurpose-built in-memory/index structure. For the interview, \nRedis/sharded in-memory index is easy to explain.\n\n\nBut how does Redis know which resources are available?\n\nThis is the more important part.\nI would not make a periodic full DB-scanning job the primary mechanism.\n\nInstead, update the Availability Index asynchronously whenever authoritative Resource state changes.\n\nThink:\n              authoritative change\n                     |\n                     v\nResource DB ----> change event / CDC ----> Index Updater ----> Redis\n\nFor example, initially:\n\nRESOURCE DB\nr101\nstate = AVAILABLE\ncpu = 8\nmemory = 32\nversion = 17\n\nThe index updater gets that change and adds:\nRedis:\npoolKey → r101\nNow r101 becomes discoverable.\nWhen the resource is reserved\nAllocator performs the authoritative CAS:\n\nr101:\nAVAILABLE/v17\n      ↓\nRESERVED/v18\n\nThe database is updated first.\n\nThen that change eventually reaches the index updater:\n\nDB change:\nr101 RESERVED\n      ↓\nIndex Updater\n      ↓\nremove r101 from Redis availability index\n\nSo eventually:\n\nRedis no longer contains r101\n\nThere can be a short period where Redis still says r101 is available.\n\nThat's exactly why we say:\n\nThe availability index may be stale.\n\nWhat happens during that stale window?\n\nSuppose:\n\nDB:\nr101 = RESERVED/v18\n\nRedis:\nr101 = AVAILABLE/v17    ← hasn't caught up yet\n\nAnother allocator searches Redis.\n\nRedis returns:\n\nr101\n\nThat's fine.\n\nThe allocator then goes to the authoritative DB:\n\nclaim r101\nif state == AVAILABLE\nand version == 17\n\nBut the DB contains:\n\nRESERVED/v18\n\nSo CAS fails.\n\nAllocator simply tries another top-K candidate:\n\nr102\n\nThis is why the design works even when Redis is eventually consistent.\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "8FQQpmV-xkjU8ZHh3879B",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5630.596703891103,
      "y": 73169.53434444392,
      "width": 581.3740103453579,
      "height": 1082.0679750823006,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bQn",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 679161045,
      "version": 653,
      "versionNonce": 1248033646,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788724199375,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What produces these change events?\nBelow are a few reasonable implementations.\n\nOption 1 — CDC\n\nResource DB\n    |\n DynamoDB Streams / DB CDC\n    |\n    v\nIndex Updater\n    |\n    v\nRedis\n\nOr:\n\nOption 2 — Transactional Outbox\n\nResource DB transaction\n   ├── update Resource\n   └── write Outbox event\n             |\n             v\n       Event Publisher\n             |\n             v\n       Index Updater\n             |\n             v\n           Redis\n",
      "fontSize": 27.05169937705751,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What produces these change events?\nBelow are a few reasonable implementations.\n\nOption 1 — CDC\n\nResource DB\n    |\n DynamoDB Streams / DB CDC\n    |\n    v\nIndex Updater\n    |\n    v\nRedis\n\nOr:\n\nOption 2 — Transactional Outbox\n\nResource DB transaction\n   ├── update Resource\n   └── write Outbox event\n             |\n             v\n       Event Publisher\n             |\n             v\n       Index Updater\n             |\n             v\n           Redis\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "y_ayFkAiNPqjcIb_518e-",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4260.409379092765,
      "y": 71994.25719896314,
      "width": 403.1526574796951,
      "height": 174.14507772682344,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bQs",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 256242997,
      "version": 418,
      "versionNonce": 1937628590,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788724199375,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "AUTHORITATIVE STORE\n- Resource + Allocation state\n- CAS/version claim\n- durable ownership\n- source of truth",
      "fontSize": 27.863212436291757,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "AUTHORITATIVE STORE\n- Resource + Allocation state\n- CAS/version claim\n- durable ownership\n- source of truth",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "d6lMKZAe7DBrH5nZGFgfF",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3968.226552505404,
      "y": 71730.86298646218,
      "width": 622.9215381460523,
      "height": 231.3463528535152,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bQt",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1059366389,
      "version": 745,
      "versionNonce": 1200748526,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788724199375,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "This store is the correctness boundary. \nCandidate discovery may be eventually \nconsistent, but the transition from \nAVAILABLE to RESERVED happens here \nusing a conditional update, so only one \nallocator can win.",
      "fontSize": 30.846180380468695,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "This store is the correctness boundary. \nCandidate discovery may be eventually \nconsistent, but the transition from \nAVAILABLE to RESERVED happens here \nusing a conditional update, so only one \nallocator can win.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "zxz_lWYn4L2ssfKZo_Tzi",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3014.466153961366,
      "y": 72673.18764762557,
      "width": 533.5158654187476,
      "height": 439.044755750545,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bR0",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1241492635,
      "version": 968,
      "versionNonce": 782813742,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788724199375,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "After reservation succeeds, we need to\nprovision resources.\nThose operations may take seconds or\nminutes. Provisioning \nof resources is done by 'Provisioner' and\nProvisioning Queue\nmakes the process asynch, and absorbs traffic\nburst that\nProvisioner might not be able to handle.\nSo: \ndurable reservation\n       ↓\nProvisioning Queue\n       ↓\nProvisioner",
      "fontSize": 23.41572030669573,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "After reservation succeeds, we need to provision resources.\nThose operations may take seconds or minutes. Provisioning \nof resources is done by 'Provisioner' and Provisioning Queue\nmakes the process asynch, and absorbs traffic burst that\nProvisioner might not be able to handle.\nSo: \ndurable reservation\n       ↓\nProvisioning Queue\n       ↓\nProvisioner",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "OjWgEZIQoeganYJPcFYql",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3625.795956445657,
      "y": 72631.46533504459,
      "width": 536.5725393155309,
      "height": 70.34044766890831,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bR1",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 662928885,
      "version": 597,
      "versionNonce": 665539694,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788724199375,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "idempotent: If queue delivers say alloc-9001 twice.\nThe provisioner should safely determine that it's \nalready provisioned and not create duplicate side effects. ",
      "fontSize": 18.757452711708876,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "idempotent: If queue delivers say alloc-9001 twice.\nThe provisioner should safely determine that it's \nalready provisioned and not create duplicate side effects. ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "-VzsxisOr-BlHxESGN6MX",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4207.638929728887,
      "y": 72256.16818598117,
      "width": 480.115931200011,
      "height": 99.40766739079494,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bR2",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1360656123,
      "version": 562,
      "versionNonce": 1818400430,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788724199375,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "If no worker can finish provisioning. \nMaybe external infrastructure is unavailable. \nThe expiry process conditionally \nmarks the allocation failed/releases the resource.",
      "fontSize": 19.88153347815899,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "If no worker can finish provisioning. \nMaybe external infrastructure is unavailable. \nThe expiry process conditionally \nmarks the allocation failed/releases the resource.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "txNV6sOu8boW9kp3ZyU0n",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3626.0024172782314,
      "y": 72798.50030344036,
      "width": 622.2070938817855,
      "height": 1084.5793489011753,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bR4",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 146608213,
      "version": 1463,
      "versionNonce": 360157422,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788724199375,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "WORKER CRASH and Reallocation Example: \n10:00:00  Queue sends alloc-9001 → Worker 17\n10:00:05  Worker configures network ✓\n10:00:10  Worker attaches disk ✓\n10:00:12  Worker crashes ✗\n\n           No ACK\n\n10:01:00  queue visibility timeout expires\n10:01:01  Queue sends alloc-9001 → Worker 24\n\nHere, Idempotency comes to play after Worker 24\npicks the job. \n\nWorker 24 will not execute every task from start\ninstead it will check if the resource alraeady allocated\nand if it has, it SKIPS that task and moves to next.\n\nEXAMPLE: Suppose provisioning a compute resource means:\n\ndesired state:\n    network = configured\n    disk = attached\n    image = installed\n    health = healthy\n    \nWorker 1 starts:\nnetwork ✓\ndisk ✓\nthen crashes.\n\nWorker 2 receives the same job.\nIt checks current state:\n\nnetwork already configured → skip\ndisk already attached      → skip\nimage missing               → install\nhealth not ready            → configure/check\n\nEventually:\nresource = fully provisioned\n\nThen Worker 2 updates the authoritative DB:\n\nalloc-9001:\nPROVISIONING → ALLOCATED\n\nand ACKs the queue message.",
      "fontSize": 18.076322481686258,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "WORKER CRASH and Reallocation Example: \n10:00:00  Queue sends alloc-9001 → Worker 17\n10:00:05  Worker configures network ✓\n10:00:10  Worker attaches disk ✓\n10:00:12  Worker crashes ✗\n\n           No ACK\n\n10:01:00  queue visibility timeout expires\n10:01:01  Queue sends alloc-9001 → Worker 24\n\nHere, Idempotency comes to play after Worker 24\npicks the job. \n\nWorker 24 will not execute every task from start\ninstead it will check if the resource alraeady allocated\nand if it has, it SKIPS that task and moves to next.\n\nEXAMPLE: Suppose provisioning a compute resource means:\n\ndesired state:\n    network = configured\n    disk = attached\n    image = installed\n    health = healthy\n    \nWorker 1 starts:\nnetwork ✓\ndisk ✓\nthen crashes.\n\nWorker 2 receives the same job.\nIt checks current state:\n\nnetwork already configured → skip\ndisk already attached      → skip\nimage missing               → install\nhealth not ready            → configure/check\n\nEventually:\nresource = fully provisioned\n\nThen Worker 2 updates the authoritative DB:\n\nalloc-9001:\nPROVISIONING → ALLOCATED\n\nand ACKs the queue message.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "n_fCToM271DMCnkPZo0To",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3630.9365522793887,
      "y": 72718.31602555267,
      "width": 473.2522212704137,
      "height": 56.35566870839858,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bR6",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1307030741,
      "version": 414,
      "versionNonce": 1047741230,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788724199375,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A Worker must verify DB state first. Before doing provisioning, \nWorker should not blindly trust the queue message. if in \nDB state != RESERVED/PROVISIONING, then ignore message",
      "fontSize": 15.02817832223962,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A Worker must verify DB state first. Before doing provisioning, \nWorker should not blindly trust the queue message. if in \nDB state != RESERVED/PROVISIONING, then ignore message",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "VEH9pkcygYE4hhO9KyPYS",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2031.1049414842187,
      "y": 73264.30598391815,
      "width": 1213.8623349967427,
      "height": 1006.1930598787766,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bR7",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 957601525,
      "version": 576,
      "versionNonce": 700362094,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788724199375,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The full request flow in simple language\n\nYou can memorize the whole architecture like this:\n\n1 Client asks for capacity.\n\n2 API validates and deduplicates the request.\n\n3 Admission decides whether the tenant is allowed to allocate.\n\n4 Allocator asks the availability index for suitable candidates.\n\n5 Allocator atomically claims one candidate in the authoritative DB.\n\n6 Once reservation is durably stored, enqueue provisioning work.\n\n7 Provisioner consumes the task and configures the resource.\n\n8 Provisioner conditionally marks the allocation ALLOCATED.\n\nIf provisioning never completes:\nReservation Expiry conditionally releases the resource.",
      "fontSize": 36.58883854104641,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The full request flow in simple language\n\nYou can memorize the whole architecture like this:\n\n1 Client asks for capacity.\n\n2 API validates and deduplicates the request.\n\n3 Admission decides whether the tenant is allowed to allocate.\n\n4 Allocator asks the availability index for suitable candidates.\n\n5 Allocator atomically claims one candidate in the authoritative DB.\n\n6 Once reservation is durably stored, enqueue provisioning work.\n\n7 Provisioner consumes the task and configures the resource.\n\n8 Provisioner conditionally marks the allocation ALLOCATED.\n\nIf provisioning never completes:\nReservation Expiry conditionally releases the resource.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cP0q1zyAbjQPPEqXpe0Wn",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4243.686133242416,
      "y": 72567.46141836724,
      "width": 273.5117890087251,
      "height": 118.30098566785225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bR8",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1618662165,
      "version": 385,
      "versionNonce": 1688391598,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788724199375,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Reservation Expiry\n- scans expired RESERVED\n- conditional release\n- reclaims leaked capacity\n- never overrides newer state",
      "fontSize": 18.92815770685636,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Reservation Expiry\n- scans expired RESERVED\n- conditional release\n- reclaims leaked capacity\n- never overrides newer state",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cwJ54TaFS7k2TwMmH14Le",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4202.3627228032665,
      "y": 72711.86647293592,
      "width": 484.72509844056617,
      "height": 267.0247612114101,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bR9",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 764348827,
      "version": 500,
      "versionNonce": 1799924206,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788724199375,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Reservations have a TTL. A background expiry process \nreclaims reservations that never complete, but release is \nconditional on the allocation still being RESERVED so a \nstale timeout cannot undo a successful allocation.\n\nI persist the reservation deadline as expiresAt on the \nauthoritative allocation record. The expiry service does \nnot scan the whole table; it uses an index on state and \nexpiration time, or time-bucketed expiry partitions at larger \nscale, to fetch only due reservations. For every candidate \nit performs a conditional state transition before releasing \nthe resource, because the reservation may have completed \nafter the expiry worker read it.”",
      "fontSize": 16.432292997625243,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Reservations have a TTL. A background expiry process \nreclaims reservations that never complete, but release is \nconditional on the allocation still being RESERVED so a \nstale timeout cannot undo a successful allocation.\n\nI persist the reservation deadline as expiresAt on the \nauthoritative allocation record. The expiry service does \nnot scan the whole table; it uses an index on state and \nexpiration time, or time-bucketed expiry partitions at larger \nscale, to fetch only due reservations. For every candidate \nit performs a conditional state transition before releasing \nthe resource, because the reservation may have completed \nafter the expiry worker read it.”",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "swzZezALQhVj6Nr7x_XcC",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1838.1926595418618,
      "y": 70932.37295133015,
      "width": 1122.444325792669,
      "height": 182.02924387800894,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
