    },
    {
      "id": "YfhGTl2Efx3dziXW-ooGz",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 483.5653521768909,
      "y": 75924.42704892368,
      "width": 1305.8657257550922,
      "height": 3142.788638265702,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bRL",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1837758779,
      "version": 1058,
      "versionNonce": 1323140718,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788724199375,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "# Functional Requirements:\nCore (must-have):\n\n- Find nearby locker with a slot that fits the pkg\n- Reserve exactly one slot \n    — no double-booking under concurrent requests\n- Keep reservation/package state in sync \n    with lockers that connect intermittently\n- Notify customer when package is ready, \n    and free the slot after pickup or expiry\n\nFollow-up (secondary, good to mention if asked):\n- Handle locker maintenance / disabled slots \n  / temporarily unavailable lockers\n- Reroute to a different locker if delivery or provisioning fails\n\n# Non-FR: \n- Strong correctness for slot ownership; \n  never assign the same slot to two active pkg.\n- High availability of cloud allocation despite \n  edge-device disconnects.\n- Low-latency locker/slot discovery across a large fleet.\n\n# BACK-OF-THE-ENVELOP\n100K lockers\n100 slots / locker ≈ 10M physical slots\n\n10M package-placement requests/day\n    ≈ 115 requests/sec average\nPeak 20x during promotions:\n    ≈ 2–3K placement requests/sec\n\nLocker heartbeat every 30 sec:\n100K / 30 ≈ 3.3K heartbeat messages/sec\n\n\n# APIs\nPOST /pkg-reservations - Find and reserve a locker slot for a package.\n\nReq: { \"packageId\": \"pkg-1001\", \"customerId\": \"cust-42\",\n  \"packageSize\": \"MEDIUM\",\n  \"destination\": {\"latitude\": 37.7749, \"longitude\": -122.4194 },\n  \"maxDistanceKm\": 5}\nResp: { \"reservationId\": \"res-901\", \"lockerId\": \"locker-201\",\n  \"slotId\": \"slot-17\", \"state\": \"RESERVED\",\n  \"expiresAt\": \"2026-09-07T18:00:00Z\" }\n\nGET  /pkg-reservations/{id} \n    - Read reservation/delivery/pickup state.\nPOST /locker-events  \n    - Locker reports door, slot, heartbeat, pickup events.\nPOST /pkg-reservations/{id}/cancel \n    - Cancel or release unused reservation.\n\n\n# DB\nLOCKER (lockerId, location, connectivityState, \n                        lastHeartbeatAt, operationalState)\n    connectivityState — ONLINE, DEGRADED, OFFLINE based on heartbeat.\n    operationalState — ACTIVE, MAINTENANCE, DISABLED.\n\nSLOT (slotId, lockerId, sizeClass, state, reservationId, version)\n     sizeClass — SMALL, MEDIUM, LARGE, etc.\n     state — AVAILABLE, RESERVED, OCCUPIED, DISABLED.\n\nPACKAGE_RESERVATION (reservationId, packageId, lockerId, \n                       slotId, state, expiresAt, notificationState)\n\nLOCKER_COMMAND (commandId, lockerId, reservationId, \n                                commandType, state, createdAt)\n    \n    commandType — PREPARE_SLOT, OPEN_DOOR, RELEASE_SLOT, etc.\n    state — PENDING, ACKED, FAILED.",
      "fontSize": 34.4415193234598,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "# Functional Requirements:\nCore (must-have):\n\n- Find nearby locker with a slot that fits the pkg\n- Reserve exactly one slot \n    — no double-booking under concurrent requests\n- Keep reservation/package state in sync \n    with lockers that connect intermittently\n- Notify customer when package is ready, \n    and free the slot after pickup or expiry\n\nFollow-up (secondary, good to mention if asked):\n- Handle locker maintenance / disabled slots \n  / temporarily unavailable lockers\n- Reroute to a different locker if delivery or provisioning fails\n\n# Non-FR: \n- Strong correctness for slot ownership; \n  never assign the same slot to two active pkg.\n- High availability of cloud allocation despite \n  edge-device disconnects.\n- Low-latency locker/slot discovery across a large fleet.\n\n# BACK-OF-THE-ENVELOP\n100K lockers\n100 slots / locker ≈ 10M physical slots\n\n10M package-placement requests/day\n    ≈ 115 requests/sec average\nPeak 20x during promotions:\n    ≈ 2–3K placement requests/sec\n\nLocker heartbeat every 30 sec:\n100K / 30 ≈ 3.3K heartbeat messages/sec\n\n\n# APIs\nPOST /pkg-reservations - Find and reserve a locker slot for a package.\n\nReq: { \"packageId\": \"pkg-1001\", \"customerId\": \"cust-42\",\n  \"packageSize\": \"MEDIUM\",\n  \"destination\": {\"latitude\": 37.7749, \"longitude\": -122.4194 },\n  \"maxDistanceKm\": 5}\nResp: { \"reservationId\": \"res-901\", \"lockerId\": \"locker-201\",\n  \"slotId\": \"slot-17\", \"state\": \"RESERVED\",\n  \"expiresAt\": \"2026-09-07T18:00:00Z\" }\n\nGET  /pkg-reservations/{id} \n    - Read reservation/delivery/pickup state.\nPOST /locker-events  \n    - Locker reports door, slot, heartbeat, pickup events.\nPOST /pkg-reservations/{id}/cancel \n    - Cancel or release unused reservation.\n\n\n# DB\nLOCKER (lockerId, location, connectivityState, \n                        lastHeartbeatAt, operationalState)\n    connectivityState — ONLINE, DEGRADED, OFFLINE based on heartbeat.\n    operationalState — ACTIVE, MAINTENANCE, DISABLED.\n\nSLOT (slotId, lockerId, sizeClass, state, reservationId, version)\n     sizeClass — SMALL, MEDIUM, LARGE, etc.\n     state — AVAILABLE, RESERVED, OCCUPIED, DISABLED.\n\nPACKAGE_RESERVATION (reservationId, packageId, lockerId, \n                       slotId, state, expiresAt, notificationState)\n\nLOCKER_COMMAND (commandId, lockerId, reservationId, \n                                commandType, state, createdAt)\n    \n    commandType — PREPARE_SLOT, OPEN_DOOR, RELEASE_SLOT, etc.\n    state — PENDING, ACKED, FAILED.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
