    {
      "id": "nEG3QFket_DYLM6kNooK1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3727.1055930695165,
      "y": 75928.16684893325,
      "width": 941.4764728535657,
      "height": 263.60353138801315,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bS7",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1431212155,
      "version": 1456,
      "versionNonce": 483439214,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788724199376,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Find nearby available locker for MEDIUM/LARGE/SMALL slot.\nA Geo+Capacity-indexed data structure (e.g., DynamoDB \nwith geohash buckets, or an OpenSearch geo index) can be used\n\nInstead of scanning 10M physical slots across 100K lockers, \nthe placement service queries this index and gets back a \nshort candidate list — maybe 10–20 lockers.",
      "fontSize": 30.126117872915792,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Find nearby available locker for MEDIUM/LARGE/SMALL slot.\nA Geo+Capacity-indexed data structure (e.g., DynamoDB \nwith geohash buckets, or an OpenSearch geo index) can be used\n\nInstead of scanning 10M physical slots across 100K lockers, \nthe placement service queries this index and gets back a \nshort candidate list — maybe 10–20 lockers.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "eUwbTPuna8j73ekYX1C0H",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3280.840207051906,
      "y": 78122.16428581455,
      "width": 1397.3347789106847,
      "height": 705.326450593402,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bS8",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 129812763,
      "version": 1533,
      "versionNonce": 288109742,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788724199376,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "HAPPY PATH — Amazon Locker Fleet Mgmt\n\n1. Delivery system requests placement (package + destination)\n2. API converts request → slot-size + location constraints\n3. Placement service queries derived availability index → gets candidate lockers\n4. Optimistic CAS reserves ONE slot (AVAILABLE→RESERVED, version-checked)\n5. Idempotent command queued to locker (durable, retried if offline)\n6. Edge gateway delivers command when locker reconnects\n7. Locker sends physical events back (door opened/package inserted/closed)\n8. Event processor updates authoritative reservation state (→ DELIVERED)\n9. Notification triggered (READY_FOR_PICKUP) — retried independently if it\nfails\n\nKEY RULE: Steps 1-4 = logical lock (cloud authoritative).\n          Steps 5-7 = physical confirmation (locker authoritative).\n          Steps 8-9 = sync + notify (never rolls back physical truth).",
      "fontSize": 35.2663225296701,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "HAPPY PATH — Amazon Locker Fleet Mgmt\n\n1. Delivery system requests placement (package + destination)\n2. API converts request → slot-size + location constraints\n3. Placement service queries derived availability index → gets candidate lockers\n4. Optimistic CAS reserves ONE slot (AVAILABLE→RESERVED, version-checked)\n5. Idempotent command queued to locker (durable, retried if offline)\n6. Edge gateway delivers command when locker reconnects\n7. Locker sends physical events back (door opened/package inserted/closed)\n8. Event processor updates authoritative reservation state (→ DELIVERED)\n9. Notification triggered (READY_FOR_PICKUP) — retried independently if it fails\n\nKEY RULE: Steps 1-4 = logical lock (cloud authoritative).\n          Steps 5-7 = physical confirmation (locker authoritative).\n          Steps 8-9 = sync + notify (never rolls back physical truth).",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "zwigxFJQAELe3UBmunIc8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4484.155479204521,
      "y": 76259.0835499566,
      "width": 816.6782758889466,
      "height": 153.03124818509013,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bS9",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 219868603,
      "version": 1252,
      "versionNonce": 1801285358,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788724199376,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What happens at step 4:\nStep 3 gave the Placement Service Top-K slots \n(e.g. slot17, slot22,...). For each candidate, in order, \nit issues a conditional update directly against the DB.",
      "fontSize": 30.606249637018017,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What happens at step 4:\nStep 3 gave the Placement Service Top-K slots \n(e.g. slot17, slot22,...). For each candidate, in order, \nit issues a conditional update directly against the DB.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "_VpAn9NG-oFw-4iln4Bcu",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2499.8613556184496,
      "y": 76880.26548555213,
      "width": 1090.3570706095975,
      "height": 242.21710431943987,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bSA",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1485536859,
      "version": 1236,
      "versionNonce": 1475174702,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788724199376,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "I don't publish to SQS directly from the reservation \nwrite path — that's a dual-write. I persist the command \nas a PENDING row in the same write as the reservation, \nand a separate Outbox Publisher (DynamoDB Streams \n+ Lambda, or a poller) reliably drains it into SQS.",
      "fontSize": 38.75473669111039,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "I don't publish to SQS directly from the reservation \nwrite path — that's a dual-write. I persist the command \nas a PENDING row in the same write as the reservation, \nand a separate Outbox Publisher (DynamoDB Streams \n+ Lambda, or a poller) reliably drains it into SQS.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "XgIwuz4YcTzPJOXj0MX1W",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1839.5990005558965,
      "y": 77387.54628710459,
      "width": 1293.2885535948528,
      "height": 314.6357623577802,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bSB",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1424030459,
      "version": 1548,
      "versionNonce": 172297070,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788724199376,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "EDGE GATEWAY - piece of infrastructure that manages persistent \nconnections to thousands of physical locker — it's the architectural \nrole of managing live, persistent connections to intermittently-connected \ndevices and routing durable cloud messages to them.  \nI'd implement it with AWS IoT Core, which gives me device identity, \nMQTT-based persistent sessions, and reconnect-aware delivery,\n rather than building that connection-management layer myself.",
      "fontSize": 35.95837284088918,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "EDGE GATEWAY - piece of infrastructure that manages persistent \nconnections to thousands of physical locker — it's the architectural \nrole of managing live, persistent connections to intermittently-connected \ndevices and routing durable cloud messages to them.  \nI'd implement it with AWS IoT Core, which gives me device identity, \nMQTT-based persistent sessions, and reconnect-aware delivery,\n rather than building that connection-management layer myself.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "emErLSQTEN2t9HA8-LSV1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3442.9824351534003,
      "y": 77593.86725951554,
      "width": 494.35366373525346,
      "height": 64.94572587245281,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
