      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "-Yxr7vxZEYCZ02I8_Pzy2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3940.0174165442027,
      "y": 77186.25554819398,
      "width": 333.021579738205,
      "height": 112.06332095196758,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bSD",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1576319035,
      "version": 1309,
      "versionNonce": 139429870,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788724199376,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "updates authoritative \nreservation state \n(→ DELIVERED)",
      "fontSize": 29.883552253858024,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "updates authoritative \nreservation state \n(→ DELIVERED)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ONBetLAOzc2ZsQHPqoxL-",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5429.308381564235,
      "y": 76445.81509491634,
      "width": 1309.3470557896433,
      "height": 1700.5413429259017,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bSE",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 818411739,
      "version": 1497,
      "versionNonce": 2054209646,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788725529678,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "COMPONENT → TECHNOLOGY MAP — Amazon Locker Fleet Mgmt\n\n[ALLOCATION]\nLocker Allocation API → Java on ECS/EKS → stateless\n  Accepts placement requests, entry point to control plane\n\n[DISCOVERY]\nLocker Placement Service   → Java service → reads eventual, writes strong\n  Filters + scores candidates, drives top-K CAS retry\n\nAvailability Index  → DynamoDB+geohash / OpenSearch geo → eventually consistent\n  Fast nearby-locker lookup, rebuildable, never grants ownership\n\n[CHECKOUT — CORRECTNESS BOUNDARY]\nSlot + Reservation Store → DynamoDB → STRONGLY consistent (CAS)\n  Only place slot ownership legally changes (state+version conditional write)\n\n[OUTBOX]\nCommand Publisher  → DynamoDB Streams + Lambda  → at-least-once\n  Drains PENDING LOCKER_COMMAND rows → queue (avoids dual-write)\n\n[EDGE DELIVERY]\nLocker Command Queue → SQS  → durable, at-least-once\n  Buffers commands while locker is offline\n\nEdge Gateway → AWS IoT Core (MQTT) → at-least-once, reconnect-aware\n  Persistent device identity + live session, routes cmd to right locker\n\n[EVENT SYNC]\nEvent Processor → ECS/EKS consumer → idempotent conditional updates\n  Dedupes device events, reconciles physical truth into authoritative state\n\n[NOTIFY — DECOUPLED]\nNotification Queue → SQS  →  → at-least-once\n  Isolates notification failures from delivery state\n\nNotification Service → SNS / Pinpoint → best-effort, independent retry\n  Push → email → SMS fallback/escalation\n\nKEY RULE: Only Slot+Reservation Store needs STRONG consistency.\n          Everything else (index, queues, gateway, notify) = eventually\n          consistent + independently retryable. No component's staleness\n          or outage can corrupt slot ownership.",
      "fontSize": 31.63797847304,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "COMPONENT → TECHNOLOGY MAP — Amazon Locker Fleet Mgmt\n\n[ALLOCATION]\nLocker Allocation API → Java on ECS/EKS → stateless\n  Accepts placement requests, entry point to control plane\n\n[DISCOVERY]\nLocker Placement Service   → Java service → reads eventual, writes strong\n  Filters + scores candidates, drives top-K CAS retry\n\nAvailability Index  → DynamoDB+geohash / OpenSearch geo → eventually consistent\n  Fast nearby-locker lookup, rebuildable, never grants ownership\n\n[CHECKOUT — CORRECTNESS BOUNDARY]\nSlot + Reservation Store → DynamoDB → STRONGLY consistent (CAS)\n  Only place slot ownership legally changes (state+version conditional write)\n\n[OUTBOX]\nCommand Publisher  → DynamoDB Streams + Lambda  → at-least-once\n  Drains PENDING LOCKER_COMMAND rows → queue (avoids dual-write)\n\n[EDGE DELIVERY]\nLocker Command Queue → SQS  → durable, at-least-once\n  Buffers commands while locker is offline\n\nEdge Gateway → AWS IoT Core (MQTT) → at-least-once, reconnect-aware\n  Persistent device identity + live session, routes cmd to right locker\n\n[EVENT SYNC]\nEvent Processor → ECS/EKS consumer → idempotent conditional updates\n  Dedupes device events, reconciles physical truth into authoritative state\n\n[NOTIFY — DECOUPLED]\nNotification Queue → SQS  →  → at-least-once\n  Isolates notification failures from delivery state\n\nNotification Service → SNS / Pinpoint → best-effort, independent retry\n  Push → email → SMS fallback/escalation\n\nKEY RULE: Only Slot+Reservation Store needs STRONG consistency.\n          Everything else (index, queues, gateway, notify) = eventually\n          consistent + independently retryable. No component's staleness\n          or outage can corrupt slot ownership.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "wzPcdvntdq8jUyHm6M7x7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4502.713382335064,
      "y": 77041.1087231349,
      "width": 796.067626953125,
      "height": 270,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bSF",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1163592370,
      "version": 94,
      "versionNonce": 136187890,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788725682984,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "This is one place where I would use an\nOutbox because there is a real dual-write\nboundary: once READY_FOR_PICKUP\ncommits, notification work must be emitted\neven if the process crashes immediately\nafterward.",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "This is one place where I would use an Outbox because there is a real dual-write boundary: once READY_FOR_PICKUP commits, notification work must be emitted even if the process crashes immediately afterward.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q7Tfgi91FjrfvYpWjXypO",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 415.33021443971677,
      "y": 79401.6664647425,
      "width": 1665.6302410887804,
      "height": 45.809424191233084,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bSH",
