    {
      "id": "a9qVA1QdHSBKGX3uTLoE_",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 455.7929992931812,
      "y": 79467.7114405348,
      "width": 811.3795776367188,
      "height": 2300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bSJ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1782668082,
      "version": 421,
      "versionNonce": 1894372111,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789964064149,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "# FR:\n- Read approx. product availability (fast, can be stale)\n- Reserve inventory atomically during checkout (NO oversell)\n- Confirm reservation → permanent sale (idempotent)\n- Release inventory on payment failure / abandonment / expiry\n    \nFOLLOW-UP/Out Of Scope\n- Fair handling of extreme flash-sale contention\n- Inventory reconciliation with fulfillment systems\n\n# Non-FR: \n- Strong consistency for inventory ownership-changing ops\n  (reserve / confirm / release — never read-then-write)\n\n- Handle extreme bursts concentrated on a very small\n  number of hot SKUs (skew, not just total QPS)\n\n- Keep read/checkout latency low while protecting the\n  inventory authority from overload\n\nONE-LINER:\n\"Strong consistency where ownership changes hands;\n everything else (availability reads) can be cheap,\n cached, and eventually consistent — the system is\n built to survive skew, not just scale.\"\n\n# Back-Of-the-envelop\n100M daily product-detail views\n\nNormal checkout:\n~10K inventory reservations/sec\n\nFlash sale:\n1M buyers target one SKU in 10 sec\n≈ 100K reservation attempts/sec for ONE SKU\n\nSuppose SKU has only 50K units:\nmost requests are guaranteed to lose.\n\n# APIs\nGET    /inventory/{sku}\n  → approximate sellable availability (cached/derived)\n\nPOST   /inventory/reservations\n  → atomically reserve qty for checkout (idempotent via requestId)\n\n Req: { \"requestId\": \"checkout-7821\", \"customerId\": \"cust-42\",\n  \"sku\": \"PS5-BUNDLE\", \"quantity\": 1, \"fulfillmentRegion\": \"us-west\"}\n\n Resp: {\"reservationId\": \"res-901\", \"sku\": \"PS5-BUNDLE\", \"qty\": 1, \n  \"state\": \"HELD\", \"expiresAt\": \"2026-09-06T21:05:00Z\"}\n\nPOST   /inventory/reservations/{id}/confirm\n  → HELD -> CONFIRMED (payment succeeded)\n\nDELETE /inventory/reservations/{id}\n  → HELD -> RELEASED (payment failed / cancelled)\n\n\n# DB\nINVENTORY\n- inventoryKey     PK (sku + fulfillmentPool [+ shard])\n- sellableQty       physical qty eligible for sale\n- reservedQty       held by active checkouts\n- committedQty      committed to confirmed orders\n- version           optimistic concurrency token (if using CAS)\n\n  (alt minimal form: availableQty + reservedQty,\n   with invariant-preserving transitions)\n\nRESERVATION\n- reservationId    PK  stable hold identity\n- requestId        UNIQUE  client idempotency key\n- inventoryKey     FK  sku/pool/shard reserved from\n- quantity\n- state            HELD | CONFIRMED | RELEASED | EXPIRED\n- expiresAt\n\nORDER\n- orderId          PK\n- reservationId     inventory hold backing this order\n- customerId\n- state            PENDING_PAYMENT | CONFIRMED | CANCELLED\n- paymentId\n\nINVENTORY_EVENT / OUTBOX   (only if commit must reliably notify downstream)\n- eventId          PK  unique publication identity\n- reservationId\n- eventType        RESERVED | CONFIRMED | RELEASED\n- published        bool\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "# FR:\n- Read approx. product availability (fast, can be stale)\n- Reserve inventory atomically during checkout (NO oversell)\n- Confirm reservation → permanent sale (idempotent)\n- Release inventory on payment failure / abandonment / expiry\n    \nFOLLOW-UP/Out Of Scope\n- Fair handling of extreme flash-sale contention\n- Inventory reconciliation with fulfillment systems\n\n# Non-FR: \n- Strong consistency for inventory ownership-changing ops\n  (reserve / confirm / release — never read-then-write)\n\n- Handle extreme bursts concentrated on a very small\n  number of hot SKUs (skew, not just total QPS)\n\n- Keep read/checkout latency low while protecting the\n  inventory authority from overload\n\nONE-LINER:\n\"Strong consistency where ownership changes hands;\n everything else (availability reads) can be cheap,\n cached, and eventually consistent — the system is\n built to survive skew, not just scale.\"\n\n# Back-Of-the-envelop\n100M daily product-detail views\n\nNormal checkout:\n~10K inventory reservations/sec\n\nFlash sale:\n1M buyers target one SKU in 10 sec\n≈ 100K reservation attempts/sec for ONE SKU\n\nSuppose SKU has only 50K units:\nmost requests are guaranteed to lose.\n\n# APIs\nGET    /inventory/{sku}\n  → approximate sellable availability (cached/derived)\n\nPOST   /inventory/reservations\n  → atomically reserve qty for checkout (idempotent via requestId)\n\n Req: { \"requestId\": \"checkout-7821\", \"customerId\": \"cust-42\",\n  \"sku\": \"PS5-BUNDLE\", \"quantity\": 1, \"fulfillmentRegion\": \"us-west\"}\n\n Resp: {\"reservationId\": \"res-901\", \"sku\": \"PS5-BUNDLE\", \"qty\": 1, \n  \"state\": \"HELD\", \"expiresAt\": \"2026-09-06T21:05:00Z\"}\n\nPOST   /inventory/reservations/{id}/confirm\n  → HELD -> CONFIRMED (payment succeeded)\n\nDELETE /inventory/reservations/{id}\n  → HELD -> RELEASED (payment failed / cancelled)\n\n\n# DB\nINVENTORY\n- inventoryKey     PK (sku + fulfillmentPool [+ shard])\n- sellableQty       physical qty eligible for sale\n- reservedQty       held by active checkouts\n- committedQty      committed to confirmed orders\n- version           optimistic concurrency token (if using CAS)\n\n  (alt minimal form: availableQty + reservedQty,\n   with invariant-preserving transitions)\n\nRESERVATION\n- reservationId    PK  stable hold identity\n- requestId        UNIQUE  client idempotency key\n- inventoryKey     FK  sku/pool/shard reserved from\n- quantity\n- state            HELD | CONFIRMED | RELEASED | EXPIRED\n- expiresAt\n\nORDER\n- orderId          PK\n- reservationId     inventory hold backing this order\n- customerId\n- state            PENDING_PAYMENT | CONFIRMED | CANCELLED\n- paymentId\n\nINVENTORY_EVENT / OUTBOX   (only if commit must reliably notify downstream)\n- eventId          PK  unique publication identity\n- reservationId\n- eventType        RESERVED | CONFIRMED | RELEASED\n- published        bool\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
