    },
    {
      "id": "DE4_VcqOOEnT4jvgGjbmV",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2489.7208669957645,
      "y": 79714.06355885549,
      "width": 586.5333251953125,
      "height": 455.14897343910263,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bTE",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2063471406,
      "version": 874,
      "versionNonce": 1139737838,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788735751377,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Why Waiting Room\nFlash-sale problem is dominated by skew, \nnot just total throughput. If 1-million buyers \ntarget a SKU with 50K units, I don't want all \n1-million requests contending on the same \ninventory key. The waiting room admits requests \nat a controlled rate and provides fairness, \nwhile the authoritative inventory reservation \nstill decides who actually gets stock.\n\nWhy not just rate-limit?\nRate limiter controls QPS, but waiting room also \npreserves customer state, fairness, admission order, \nand retry identity. For a normal traffic spike rate \nlimiting may be enough; for a flash sale I’d use \nthe richer waiting-room semantics.",
      "fontSize": 22.75744867195513,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Why Waiting Room\nFlash-sale problem is dominated by skew, \nnot just total throughput. If 1-million buyers \ntarget a SKU with 50K units, I don't want all \n1-million requests contending on the same \ninventory key. The waiting room admits requests \nat a controlled rate and provides fairness, \nwhile the authoritative inventory reservation \nstill decides who actually gets stock.\n\nWhy not just rate-limit?\nRate limiter controls QPS, but waiting room also \npreserves customer state, fairness, admission order, \nand retry identity. For a normal traffic spike rate \nlimiting may be enough; for a flash sale I’d use \nthe richer waiting-room semantics.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Thmxq8P_hdnYFZbioe42y",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1338.8119515112194,
      "y": 80136.60410758975,
      "width": 587.9666748046875,
      "height": 85.73518265878442,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bTF",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 745504110,
      "version": 366,
      "versionNonce": 1517455854,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788735800669,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Inventory reservation service atomically decrements \nsellable availability or increments reserved qty only \nif enough stock remains.",
      "fontSize": 22.862715375675847,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Inventory reservation service atomically decrements \nsellable availability or increments reserved qty only \nif enough stock remains.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "VGsJwtrF07dk4jtXfZAEV",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1907.2591419692149,
      "y": 80693.6755036789,
      "width": 785.7408014920069,
      "height": 519.6202819463389,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bTG",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2025430958,
      "version": 358,
      "versionNonce": 864665454,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788735814570,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "HAPPY-PATH WALKTHROUGH\n1. Browse            → Checkout API reads Availability Cache (stale OK)\n2. Checkout attempt  → enters Flash Sale Admission / Waiting Room\n3. Admitted request  → reaches Inventory Reservation Service\n4. Atomic hold       → Inventory Store (AUTHORITATIVE) — reserve\n5. Hold → Order      → Order Service creates order against reservation\n6. Order → Payment   → Payment Service processes payment\n7. Payment success   → HELD -> CONFIRMED\n8. Payment failure   → HELD -> RELEASED (+ restore qty)\n\nPHASES:\n  1-2  cheap / stale-tolerant   (cache + admission gate)\n  3-4  strict / strongly consistent  (the ONE hold moment)\n  5-8  slow / external          (order + payment, OUTSIDE inventory txn)\n\nONE-LINER:\n\"Secure the unit fast (steps 3-4), then do the slow stuff\n (payment) only after it's already safe — never hold\n inventory open while waiting on an external gateway.\"",
      "fontSize": 21.878748713530054,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "HAPPY-PATH WALKTHROUGH\n1. Browse            → Checkout API reads Availability Cache (stale OK)\n2. Checkout attempt  → enters Flash Sale Admission / Waiting Room\n3. Admitted request  → reaches Inventory Reservation Service\n4. Atomic hold       → Inventory Store (AUTHORITATIVE) — reserve\n5. Hold → Order      → Order Service creates order against reservation\n6. Order → Payment   → Payment Service processes payment\n7. Payment success   → HELD -> CONFIRMED\n8. Payment failure   → HELD -> RELEASED (+ restore qty)\n\nPHASES:\n  1-2  cheap / stale-tolerant   (cache + admission gate)\n  3-4  strict / strongly consistent  (the ONE hold moment)\n  5-8  slow / external          (order + payment, OUTSIDE inventory txn)\n\nONE-LINER:\n\"Secure the unit fast (steps 3-4), then do the slow stuff\n (payment) only after it's already safe — never hold\n inventory open while waiting on an external gateway.\"",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "hTPOrj2Btvs99pwPgNZaW",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3254.4292926925136,
      "y": 79579.90594134456,
      "width": 706.1601016537612,
      "height": 884.7481552042487,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bTH",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1946515950,
      "version": 250,
      "versionNonce": 1571801198,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788735747143,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "PREVENT OVERSELLING\nSETUP: availableQty = 1, two buyers arrive simultaneously\n\nWRONG (read-then-write / TOCTOU race):\n  read availableQty\n  if > 0: write availableQty - 1\n  → both can read 1, both decrement → oversell / negative qty\n\nRIGHT (atomic conditional mutation):\n  UPDATE Inventory\n  SET availableQty = availableQty - 1\n  WHERE inventoryKey = ?\n    AND availableQty >= 1;\n\n  DynamoDB:\n  UpdateItem SET availableQty = availableQty - :q\n             Condition: availableQty >= :q\n  → fails with ConditionalCheckFailedException if not enough stock\n\nWHY IT WORKS:\n  check + mutation = ONE atomic op in the datastore.\n  No gap for two requests to both \"pass.\" Exactly one\n  concurrent update succeeds; all others' condition\n  fails and are rejected outright.\n\nDOES NOT SOLVE:\n  hot-key throughput under massive contention (→ §14/§16:\n  admission + sharding — a separate problem)\n\nONE-LINER:\n\"Never read-then-write for inventory. The decrement\n itself is the check — atomic in the store, not split\n across two application-level round-trips.\"",
      "fontSize": 21.448440126163607,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "PREVENT OVERSELLING\nSETUP: availableQty = 1, two buyers arrive simultaneously\n\nWRONG (read-then-write / TOCTOU race):\n  read availableQty\n  if > 0: write availableQty - 1\n  → both can read 1, both decrement → oversell / negative qty\n\nRIGHT (atomic conditional mutation):\n  UPDATE Inventory\n  SET availableQty = availableQty - 1\n  WHERE inventoryKey = ?\n    AND availableQty >= 1;\n\n  DynamoDB:\n  UpdateItem SET availableQty = availableQty - :q\n             Condition: availableQty >= :q\n  → fails with ConditionalCheckFailedException if not enough stock\n\nWHY IT WORKS:\n  check + mutation = ONE atomic op in the datastore.\n  No gap for two requests to both \"pass.\" Exactly one\n  concurrent update succeeds; all others' condition\n  fails and are rejected outright.\n\nDOES NOT SOLVE:\n  hot-key throughput under massive contention (→ §14/§16:\n  admission + sharding — a separate problem)\n\nONE-LINER:\n\"Never read-then-write for inventory. The decrement\n itself is the check — atomic in the store, not split\n across two application-level round-trips.\"",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "_Nc-_CHLnxAHAHlPbERN7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3254.4292926925136,
      "y": 80532.47952112913,
      "width": 576.9871457404731,
      "height": 804.2796107932245,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bTI",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1163660334,
      "version": 297,
      "versionNonce": 1724649970,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788735743333,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "# HOT SKU STRATEGIES\nOPTION 1 — ADMISSION TOKENS (§15)\n  Problem:  1M buyers, 50K units → don't let all 1M\n            hit inventory directly\n  Fix:      Issue ~50K (+ small margin) admission tokens\n            via waiting room; only token-holders may\n            attempt reservation\n  Key rule: Token = permission to ATTEMPT, not ownership.\n            Real correctness check still happens at the\n            authoritative inventory decrement.\n\nOPTION 2 — SHARD INVENTORY (§16)\n  Problem:  One inventory counter/partition becomes a\n            hot key even with correct atomic decrement\n  Fix:      Split stock into N shards\n            (e.g. PS5#0..PS5#9, 5K units each)\n            Requests hash/spread across shards.\n            Global availability = sum(shard qtys)\n  Trade-off: Uneven depletion — one shard may hit zero\n             while others still have stock. On failure,\n             retry a different shard.\n\nRELATIONSHIP:\n  Admission  → controls HOW MANY requests reach inventory\n  Sharding   → controls HOW FAST inventory can absorb\n               the requests that do arrive\n  Different problems. Use BOTH at extreme scale.\n\nMENTAL MODEL:\n\"Bouncer at the door (admission) + ten registers\n instead of one (sharding). Bouncer thins the crowd;\n multiple registers process it faster. Neither alone\n survives a true Prime Day spike.\"",
      "fontSize": 19.49768753438119,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "# HOT SKU STRATEGIES\nOPTION 1 — ADMISSION TOKENS (§15)\n  Problem:  1M buyers, 50K units → don't let all 1M\n            hit inventory directly\n  Fix:      Issue ~50K (+ small margin) admission tokens\n            via waiting room; only token-holders may\n            attempt reservation\n  Key rule: Token = permission to ATTEMPT, not ownership.\n            Real correctness check still happens at the\n            authoritative inventory decrement.\n\nOPTION 2 — SHARD INVENTORY (§16)\n  Problem:  One inventory counter/partition becomes a\n            hot key even with correct atomic decrement\n  Fix:      Split stock into N shards\n            (e.g. PS5#0..PS5#9, 5K units each)\n            Requests hash/spread across shards.\n            Global availability = sum(shard qtys)\n  Trade-off: Uneven depletion — one shard may hit zero\n             while others still have stock. On failure,\n             retry a different shard.\n\nRELATIONSHIP:\n  Admission  → controls HOW MANY requests reach inventory\n  Sharding   → controls HOW FAST inventory can absorb\n               the requests that do arrive\n  Different problems. Use BOTH at extreme scale.\n\nMENTAL MODEL:\n\"Bouncer at the door (admission) + ten registers\n instead of one (sharding). Bouncer thins the crowd;\n multiple registers process it faster. Neither alone\n survives a true Prime Day spike.\"",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "KFlXQhqGyLv9s7ZMM6K0p",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -762.3935284246891,
      "y": 13909.340839624467,
      "width": 1885.9598422193294,
      "height": 441.0606853176199,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bTK",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1175934703,
      "version": 290,
      "versionNonce": 1735707073,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788930182696,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "This was not just a CRUD service connected to Kafka. I designed \nthe authoritative transactional write path, reliable event-publication \nmechanism, asynchronous event distribution, and analytical data platform \nas one end-to-end architecture. \n\nThe main design challenges were consistency between the database and Kafka, \nreplay/idempotency, schema evolution, failure recovery, scaling consumers independently, \nand keeping operational and analytical workloads decoupled.",
      "fontSize": 44.10606853176197,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "This was not just a CRUD service connected to Kafka. I designed \nthe authoritative transactional write path, reliable event-publication \nmechanism, asynchronous event distribution, and analytical data platform \nas one end-to-end architecture. \n\nThe main design challenges were consistency between the database and Kafka, \nreplay/idempotency, schema evolution, failure recovery, scaling consumers independently, \nand keeping operational and analytical workloads decoupled.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "PzpQjJjCQ2C4Mm3GYlHy3",
