    },
    {
      "id": "unafhjsE0jkeNCVHr1L5b",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 496.764513082745,
      "y": 82484.16082790773,
      "width": 668.5995483398438,
      "height": 1400,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bUK",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 357857537,
      "version": 424,
      "versionNonce": 1875540207,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790023283508,
      "created": 1789964086411,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "# Functional\n- Upload video\n- watch video\n\nBelow the line (out of scope)\nview information about a video, such as view counts.\nsearch for videos.\ncomment on videos.\nsee recommended videos.\nmake a channel and manage their channel.\nsubscribe to channels.\n\n# Non-Functional\n- Availability > Consistency\n- Low latency streaming, even in low bandwidth environments.\n- support uploading, streaming large videos (10s of GBs).\n- should scale to a high number of videos uploaded, watched per day\n- Should support resumable uploads\n\n# Back-of-the-envelop\n100M daily viewers × 10 plays/day\n≈ 1B plays/day\n≈ 12K average playback starts/sec\n≈ 50K–100K/sec at peak\n\n5M uploads/day × 200 MB average\n≈ 1 PB/day raw uploaded video\n\nWith multiple encoded renditions:\n≈ 2–3 PB/day of generated video objects\n\n\n# DB\nUser: A user of the system (uploader or viewer).\nVideo: A video that is uploaded / watched.\nVideoMetadata: This is metadata associated with the video, \n    such as the uploading user, URL reference to a transcript, etc. \n    - videoId, uploader_Id, name, desc, chunks, s3_url  \n\n# API\n- To upload a video, server will create a pre-signed URL to enable \n  the client to upload directly to S3. The request payload will just \n  be the video metadata.\n    POST /presigned_url\n    Request:\n    {Video, VideoMetadata}\n    \n- POST /presigned_url\n    Request:\n    { Video, VideoMetadata }\n\n- To stream a video, retrieve the video data to play it on device:\n    GET /videos/{videoId} -> Resp: {VideoMetadata}\n        VideoMetadata, will contain URL(s) necessary to watch video.\n    \n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "# Functional\n- Upload video\n- watch video\n\nBelow the line (out of scope)\nview information about a video, such as view counts.\nsearch for videos.\ncomment on videos.\nsee recommended videos.\nmake a channel and manage their channel.\nsubscribe to channels.\n\n# Non-Functional\n- Availability > Consistency\n- Low latency streaming, even in low bandwidth environments.\n- support uploading, streaming large videos (10s of GBs).\n- should scale to a high number of videos uploaded, watched per day\n- Should support resumable uploads\n\n# Back-of-the-envelop\n100M daily viewers × 10 plays/day\n≈ 1B plays/day\n≈ 12K average playback starts/sec\n≈ 50K–100K/sec at peak\n\n5M uploads/day × 200 MB average\n≈ 1 PB/day raw uploaded video\n\nWith multiple encoded renditions:\n≈ 2–3 PB/day of generated video objects\n\n\n# DB\nUser: A user of the system (uploader or viewer).\nVideo: A video that is uploaded / watched.\nVideoMetadata: This is metadata associated with the video, \n    such as the uploading user, URL reference to a transcript, etc. \n    - videoId, uploader_Id, name, desc, chunks, s3_url  \n\n# API\n- To upload a video, server will create a pre-signed URL to enable \n  the client to upload directly to S3. The request payload will just \n  be the video metadata.\n    POST /presigned_url\n    Request:\n    {Video, VideoMetadata}\n    \n- POST /presigned_url\n    Request:\n    { Video, VideoMetadata }\n\n- To stream a video, retrieve the video data to play it on device:\n    GET /videos/{videoId} -> Resp: {VideoMetadata}\n        VideoMetadata, will contain URL(s) necessary to watch video.\n    \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
