    {
      "id": "6I9kJGiPh0UelEOPdi5iV",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1974.536185146936,
      "y": 83134.58686703943,
      "width": 224.46915239041257,
      "height": 80.88791658863192,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bVb",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1964981793,
      "version": 465,
      "versionNonce": 92045121,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790022185082,
      "created": 1790022038324,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "* Stateless service handling:\n  * Presigned URL requests\n  * Video metadata point queries\n* Horizontally scalable behind a LB.\n* Since no session state is stored locally, \n   requests can be routed to any instance.",
      "fontSize": 10.785055545150918,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "* Stateless service handling:\n  * Presigned URL requests\n  * Video metadata point queries\n* Horizontally scalable behind a LB.\n* Since no session state is stored locally, \n   requests can be routed to any instance.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "6FTvqfYiVE15ScYp8HUZp",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1973.1304452297086,
      "y": 83263.6878199074,
      "width": 361.6156921386719,
      "height": 240,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bVc",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1388802607,
      "version": 120,
      "versionNonce": 1641235407,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790022361881,
      "created": 1790022289869,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Video Metadata (Cassandra)\n* Stores video metadata, \n  partitioned by `videoId`.\n* Scales horizontally using:\n  * Leaderless replication\n  * Consistent hashing\n* `videoId` partitioning provides \n   generally uniform data distribution.\n* **Hot-video risk:** If a very popular \n   video's partition is concentrated on a small \n   replica set, those Cassandra nodes can \n   become hot and create a bottleneck.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Video Metadata (Cassandra)\n* Stores video metadata, \n  partitioned by `videoId`.\n* Scales horizontally using:\n  * Leaderless replication\n  * Consistent hashing\n* `videoId` partitioning provides \n   generally uniform data distribution.\n* **Hot-video risk:** If a very popular \n   video's partition is concentrated on a small \n   replica set, those Cassandra nodes can \n   become hot and create a bottleneck.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "3CWBY4GW8xTTCLwjnqa8z",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2897.3040308143695,
      "y": 83256.36775203483,
      "width": 518.07958984375,
      "height": 220,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bVd",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1148914721,
      "version": 9,
      "versionNonce": 998901377,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790022437997,
      "created": 1790022415075,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "### Video Processing Service\n\n* Processes uploaded videos using distributed worker nodes.\n* Can coordinate DAG-based processing tasks such as:\n  * Transcoding\n  * Thumbnail generation\n  * Multiple resolutions/formats\n* Uses an internal durable queue to absorb upload bursts.\n* Workers consume jobs asynchronously.\n* Queue depth / pending-job count can be used as an autoscaling \n  signal to add or remove workers.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "### Video Processing Service\n\n* Processes uploaded videos using distributed worker nodes.\n* Can coordinate DAG-based processing tasks such as:\n  * Transcoding\n  * Thumbnail generation\n  * Multiple resolutions/formats\n* Uses an internal durable queue to absorb upload bursts.\n* Workers consume jobs asynchronously.\n* Queue depth / pending-job count can be used as an autoscaling \n  signal to add or remove workers.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "k_A8HMxTCOyGWU2itIUmS",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2269.994159490086,
      "y": 82463.44437300808,
      "width": 370.54618940282825,
      "height": 267.3701042764588,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bVs",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1589345153,
      "version": 216,
      "versionNonce": 1182309231,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790022625853,
      "created": 1790022602386,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "### S3 — Video/Object Storage\n\n* Stores original and processed video files.\n* Scales to very high traffic and object volumes.\n* An S3 bucket is regional and automatically \n  replicated across multiple AZs within that region.\n* For global delivery, use:\n\n  * CDN for edge caching, and/or\n  * Cross-region replication when geo-distributed \n    copies are required.\n* **Latency risk:** If users are far from the S3 region, \n     direct streaming from S3 can increase startup latency \n     and buffering.\n* **Solution:** Serve popular/video content through a \n     geographically distributed CDN, keeping S3 as the origin.\n",
      "fontSize": 12.582122554186292,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "### S3 — Video/Object Storage\n\n* Stores original and processed video files.\n* Scales to very high traffic and object volumes.\n* An S3 bucket is regional and automatically \n  replicated across multiple AZs within that region.\n* For global delivery, use:\n\n  * CDN for edge caching, and/or\n  * Cross-region replication when geo-distributed \n    copies are required.\n* **Latency risk:** If users are far from the S3 region, \n     direct streaming from S3 can increase startup latency \n     and buffering.\n* **Solution:** Serve popular/video content through a \n     geographically distributed CDN, keeping S3 as the origin.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "IiXaAvZ3tZJSctzT-fheM",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3651.7211509871195,
      "y": 82447.44147236309,
      "width": 762.4194946289062,
      "height": 1325,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bVt",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 92853857,
      "version": 311,
      "versionNonce": 1402709633,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790023136557,
      "created": 1790022992848,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "### Handling Hot / Viral Videos\n\nA viral video creates an extreme **read hotspot**: \nit may be uploaded once but viewed millions of times.\n\nTo handle this:\n\n* **Cache metadata aggressively**\n\n  * Use a distributed cache such as **Redis / Memcached**.\n  * Key by `videoId`.\n  * Cache hot video metadata to avoid repeatedly hitting Cassandra.\n  * Use TTL/LRU-style eviction.\n\n* **Leverage Cassandra replication**\n\n  * Cassandra already replicates each partition across multiple nodes.\n  * Tune the **replication factor and read consistency** \n     so reads can be served from multiple replicas.\n  * This reduces pressure on a single replica set, although \n    extremely hot keys can still create hotspots.\n\n* **Use CDN for actual video content**\n\n  * Store video files in S3, but serve them through a CDN \n    such as **CloudFront / Akamai**.\n  * Viral videos are cached at edge locations close to users.\n  * This prevents repeated requests from reaching S3 and \n    reduces latency and buffering.\n\n* **Scale stateless read services**\n  * Video Service remains stateless and horizontally scales \n    behind a load balancer.\n\n### Interview Script\n\n> “The key issue with a viral video is that the system becomes \n   extremely read-heavy. A video may be written once but read \n   millions of times.\n\n> For metadata, I would first serve hot entries from a distributed \n  cache like Redis, keyed by videoId, so most requests never reach Cassandra.\n\n> Cassandra already replicates partitions, so I would tune replication \n  and read consistency to distribute database reads across replicas.\n\n> For the actual video bytes, the main solution is the CDN. Popular \n  videos get cached at edge locations, so viewers are served close \n  to their geography instead of repeatedly hitting S3.\n\n> So the main scaling strategy is: **cache metadata, CDN-cache \n  video content, and horizontally scale the stateless read path.**”\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "### Handling Hot / Viral Videos\n\nA viral video creates an extreme **read hotspot**: \nit may be uploaded once but viewed millions of times.\n\nTo handle this:\n\n* **Cache metadata aggressively**\n\n  * Use a distributed cache such as **Redis / Memcached**.\n  * Key by `videoId`.\n  * Cache hot video metadata to avoid repeatedly hitting Cassandra.\n  * Use TTL/LRU-style eviction.\n\n* **Leverage Cassandra replication**\n\n  * Cassandra already replicates each partition across multiple nodes.\n  * Tune the **replication factor and read consistency** \n     so reads can be served from multiple replicas.\n  * This reduces pressure on a single replica set, although \n    extremely hot keys can still create hotspots.\n\n* **Use CDN for actual video content**\n\n  * Store video files in S3, but serve them through a CDN \n    such as **CloudFront / Akamai**.\n  * Viral videos are cached at edge locations close to users.\n  * This prevents repeated requests from reaching S3 and \n    reduces latency and buffering.\n\n* **Scale stateless read services**\n  * Video Service remains stateless and horizontally scales \n    behind a load balancer.\n\n### Interview Script\n\n> “The key issue with a viral video is that the system becomes \n   extremely read-heavy. A video may be written once but read \n   millions of times.\n\n> For metadata, I would first serve hot entries from a distributed \n  cache like Redis, keyed by videoId, so most requests never reach Cassandra.\n\n> Cassandra already replicates partitions, so I would tune replication \n  and read consistency to distribute database reads across replicas.\n\n> For the actual video bytes, the main solution is the CDN. Popular \n  videos get cached at edge locations, so viewers are served close \n  to their geography instead of repeatedly hitting S3.\n\n> So the main scaling strategy is: **cache metadata, CDN-cache \n  video content, and horizontally scale the stateless read path.**”\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
