      "created": 1790056647279,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "# Functional\n- view upcoming events\n- search upcoming events\n- book upcoming events\n\nBelow the line (out of scope)\n- view their booked events\n- Admins flow (adding, editing, etc)\n- Dynamic pricing for popular events\n\n# Non-Functional\n- Availability for searching & viewing events, \n   prioritize consistency for booking events \n   (no double booking)\n- handle popular events (10 million users, one event)\n- low latency search (< 500ms)\n- Read >> write (read heavy)\n\nBelow the line (out of scope): system should, \n- adhere to GDPR\n- fault tolerant\n- secure transactions for purchases\n- regular backups\n\n# Back-of-the-envelop\n\n\n# DB\n- Events: stores info about an event, including \n  details like date, description, type, and the \n  performer/team involved.\n  (id, venueId, performerId, name, desc)\n- Users: \n- Performer: performer's name, a brief description, \n  and potentially links to their work or profiles.\n- Venues: (id,location,seatMap...)\n  physical location where an event is held.\n- Tickets: \n    (id, eventId, seat, price, status:booked, available)\n  Info of individual tickets, event ID, \n  seat details, pricing, and status (available/sold). \n  When an event is created, tickets are generated \n  from the venue's seat map. Client combines Venue \n  seat-map data + Ticket status to render \n  interactive seat selection.\n\n- Bookings: (userId, ticketId, total_price, \n    booking_status (in-progress/confirmed)). \n\n\n# API\n- GET /events/:eventId -> Event,Venue,Performer,Ticket[]\n  tickets are to render the seat map on the Client \n- GET /events/search?\n         keyword={keyword}&start={start_date}&end={end_date}\n         &pageSize={page_size}&page={page_number} -> Event[]  \n- POST /bookings/:eventId -> bookingId\n     {\n       \"ticketIds\": string[], \n       \"paymentDetails\": ...\n     } \n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "# Functional\n- view upcoming events\n- search upcoming events\n- book upcoming events\n\nBelow the line (out of scope)\n- view their booked events\n- Admins flow (adding, editing, etc)\n- Dynamic pricing for popular events\n\n# Non-Functional\n- Availability for searching & viewing events, \n   prioritize consistency for booking events \n   (no double booking)\n- handle popular events (10 million users, one event)\n- low latency search (< 500ms)\n- Read >> write (read heavy)\n\nBelow the line (out of scope): system should, \n- adhere to GDPR\n- fault tolerant\n- secure transactions for purchases\n- regular backups\n\n# Back-of-the-envelop\n\n\n# DB\n- Events: stores info about an event, including \n  details like date, description, type, and the \n  performer/team involved.\n  (id, venueId, performerId, name, desc)\n- Users: \n- Performer: performer's name, a brief description, \n  and potentially links to their work or profiles.\n- Venues: (id,location,seatMap...)\n  physical location where an event is held.\n- Tickets: \n    (id, eventId, seat, price, status:booked, available)\n  Info of individual tickets, event ID, \n  seat details, pricing, and status (available/sold). \n  When an event is created, tickets are generated \n  from the venue's seat map. Client combines Venue \n  seat-map data + Ticket status to render \n  interactive seat selection.\n\n- Bookings: (userId, ticketId, total_price, \n    booking_status (in-progress/confirmed)). \n\n\n# API\n- GET /events/:eventId -> Event,Venue,Performer,Ticket[]\n  tickets are to render the seat map on the Client \n- GET /events/search?\n         keyword={keyword}&start={start_date}&end={end_date}\n         &pageSize={page_size}&page={page_number} -> Event[]  \n- POST /bookings/:eventId -> bookingId\n     {\n       \"ticketIds\": string[], \n       \"paymentDetails\": ...\n     } \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
