      "created": 1793732450370,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "## Core Data Models — Load Scheduling & Capacity Management\n\n### 1. VEHICLE — Truck Capacity & Availability\n\n**Purpose:** Authoritative truck metadata, capacity limits, and scheduling eligibility.\n\n- `vehicleId`, `tenantId` — Truck identity and fleet ownership.\n- `maxWeightKg`, `maxVolumeM3` — Maximum cargo capacity.\n- `status` — Available, active, out of service.\n- `scheduleVersion` — Optimistic locking to prevent concurrent route updates from overwriting each other.\n\n### 2. LOAD — Shipment Request\n\n**Purpose:** Defines what must be transported, where, and when.\n\n- `loadId`, `tenantId` — Shipment identity and fleet ownership.\n- `weightKg`, `volumeM3` — Required truck capacity.\n- `pickup` — Location + pickup time window.\n- `dropoff` — Destination + delivery time window.\n- `status` — Pending, assigned, in transit, delivered, cancelled.\n\n### 3. ASSIGNMENT — Load-to-Truck Reservation\n\n**Purpose:** Authoritative mapping of a shipment to a truck, tracking its lifecycle.\n\n- `assignmentId` — Unique assignment identity.\n- `loadId` — Assigned shipment; unique active-assignment constraint prevents double booking.\n- `vehicleId` — Truck with reserved capacity.\n- `status` — Reserved, accepted, picked up, delivered, cancelled.\n- `plannedPickupTime`, `plannedDeliveryTime` — Scheduled execution times.\n\n### 4. ROUTE_STOP — Ordered Pickup & Drop-off Schedule\n\n**Purpose:** Defines the sequence of stops used to validate truck capacity and delivery time windows.\n\n- `vehicleId`, `assignmentId` — Truck and associated shipment.\n- `stopOrder` — Execution order within the route.\n- `stopType` — Pickup or drop-off.\n- `location` — Stop coordinates.\n- `plannedTime` — Expected arrival/service time, validated against the required time window.",
      "fontSize": 22.760384806455406,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "## Core Data Models — Load Scheduling & Capacity Management\n\n### 1. VEHICLE — Truck Capacity & Availability\n\n**Purpose:** Authoritative truck metadata, capacity limits, and scheduling eligibility.\n\n- `vehicleId`, `tenantId` — Truck identity and fleet ownership.\n- `maxWeightKg`, `maxVolumeM3` — Maximum cargo capacity.\n- `status` — Available, active, out of service.\n- `scheduleVersion` — Optimistic locking to prevent concurrent route updates from overwriting each other.\n\n### 2. LOAD — Shipment Request\n\n**Purpose:** Defines what must be transported, where, and when.\n\n- `loadId`, `tenantId` — Shipment identity and fleet ownership.\n- `weightKg`, `volumeM3` — Required truck capacity.\n- `pickup` — Location + pickup time window.\n- `dropoff` — Destination + delivery time window.\n- `status` — Pending, assigned, in transit, delivered, cancelled.\n\n### 3. ASSIGNMENT — Load-to-Truck Reservation\n\n**Purpose:** Authoritative mapping of a shipment to a truck, tracking its lifecycle.\n\n- `assignmentId` — Unique assignment identity.\n- `loadId` — Assigned shipment; unique active-assignment constraint prevents double booking.\n- `vehicleId` — Truck with reserved capacity.\n- `status` — Reserved, accepted, picked up, delivered, cancelled.\n- `plannedPickupTime`, `plannedDeliveryTime` — Scheduled execution times.\n\n### 4. ROUTE_STOP — Ordered Pickup & Drop-off Schedule\n\n**Purpose:** Defines the sequence of stops used to validate truck capacity and delivery time windows.\n\n- `vehicleId`, `assignmentId` — Truck and associated shipment.\n- `stopOrder` — Execution order within the route.\n- `stopType` — Pickup or drop-off.\n- `location` — Stop coordinates.\n- `plannedTime` — Expected arrival/service time, validated against the required time window.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    }
  ],
